### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### API C2 — Agendamento de Serviços (Faesa) — Coleção de requisições
### Formato: REST Client (humao.rest-client) para VS Code.
### Também importável no Postman / Insomnia ("Import → Raw text → HTTP").
###
### Fluxo recomendado de execução (de cima para baixo):
###   1. health
###   2. register USER + login USER             → captura @userToken / @userId
###   3. register ADMIN + promote (via Prisma)  → ver bloco "ADMIN" abaixo
###   4. login ADMIN                            → captura @adminToken
###   5. create professional (com USER)         → captura @professionalId
###   6. create service                         → captura @serviceId
###   7. create appointment                     → captura @appointmentId
###   8. fluxo de ownership / 403 / soft delete
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3050
# Em produção, troque por: @baseUrl = https://api-c2.gmcsistemas.com.br

# Credenciais de exemplo — altere se já existirem no banco
@userEmail = ana.cliente@example.com
@userPassword = senha12345
@userName = Ana Cliente

@adminEmail = admin@example.com
@adminPassword = adminseguro123
@adminName = Admin Root

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Health & Docs
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Healthcheck
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### Spec OpenAPI (Swagger UI: abra {{baseUrl}}/docs no navegador)
GET {{baseUrl}}/docs/

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 1. AUTH — register / login / me / refresh
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1.1 Register USER (201)
# @name registerUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "name": "{{userName}}",
  "password": "{{userPassword}}"
}

### 1.2 Register USER — e-mail duplicado (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "name": "{{userName}}",
  "password": "{{userPassword}}"
}

### 1.3 Register — senha curta (422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "curto@example.com",
  "name": "Curto",
  "password": "123"
}

### 1.4 Login USER (200) — captura accessToken/refreshToken
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "{{userPassword}}"
}

@userToken = {{loginUser.response.body.accessToken}}
@userRefresh = {{loginUser.response.body.refreshToken}}
@userId = {{loginUser.response.body.user.id}}

### 1.5 Login — credencial inválida (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "senha-errada"
}

### 1.6 GET /auth/me sem token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 1.7 GET /auth/me com token (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 1.8 Refresh tokens (200)
# @name refreshTokens
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{userRefresh}}"
}

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 2. ADMIN — registrar e promover
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###
### O endpoint /auth/register só cria USER. Para obter um ADMIN no ambiente
### local, promova manualmente via Prisma Studio ou rode:
###
###   PowerShell:
###   npx prisma studio                    # UI: edite User.role = 'ADMIN'
###
###   ou via SQL:
###   sqlite3 prisma/dev.db "UPDATE User SET role='ADMIN' WHERE email='admin@example.com';"
###
###   ou rode o seed (cria um admin pré-configurado):
###   npm run prisma:seed
###
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 2.1 Register ADMIN (cria como USER; promova depois)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "name": "{{adminName}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 2.2 Login ADMIN (após promoção)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 3. USERS — ADMIN-only + ownership
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 3.1 GET /users sem ADMIN (403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 3.2 GET /users como ADMIN (200) — paginado
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3.3 GET /users?search= (filtro)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?search=ana
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3.4 GET /users/:id pelo próprio dono (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 3.5 GET /users/:id de outro usuário sem ADMIN (403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/algum-outro-id
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 3.6 DELETE /users/:id pelo próprio dono (204) — soft delete
# CUIDADO: invalida o {{userToken}}. Refaça o registro/login para continuar.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 4. PROFESSIONALS — CRUD + rota pública com include
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 4.1 POST /professionals — USER autenticado cria perfil profissional (201)
# @name createProfessional
POST {{baseUrl}}/professionals
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "specialty": "Psicologia clínica",
  "bio": "Atendimento adulto e adolescente, abordagem cognitivo-comportamental."
}

@professionalId = {{createProfessional.response.body.id}}

### 4.2 POST /professionals duplicado para o mesmo user (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/professionals
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "specialty": "Tentando de novo"
}

### 4.3 GET /professionals (público, paginado)
GET {{baseUrl}}/professionals?page=1&limit=10

### 4.4 GET /professionals?search=psico (filtro por especialidade)
GET {{baseUrl}}/professionals?search=psico

### 4.5 GET /professionals/:id (público, include de user + services)
GET {{baseUrl}}/professionals/{{professionalId}}

### 4.6 GET /professionals/:id inexistente (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/professionals/nao-existe-id

### 4.7 PATCH /professionals/:id pelo dono (200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/professionals/{{professionalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bio": "Atualização: atendimento online e presencial."
}

### 4.8 PATCH /professionals/:id por terceiro (403)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/professionals/{{professionalId}}
Authorization: Bearer SEU_OUTRO_TOKEN_AQUI
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bio": "Tentativa indevida"
}

### 4.9 DELETE /professionals/:id pelo dono (204) — soft delete
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/professionals/{{professionalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 5. SERVICES — CRUD (público em leitura, ownership em escrita)
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 5.1 POST /services — só quem tem perfil profissional cria (201)
# @name createService
POST {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sessão de terapia 50min",
  "description": "Atendimento individual presencial ou online.",
  "durationMin": 50,
  "priceCents": 18000
}

@serviceId = {{createService.response.body.id}}

### 5.2 POST /services com preço negativo (422 — Zod)
POST {{baseUrl}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Inválido",
  "durationMin": 30,
  "priceCents": -1
}

### 5.3 GET /services (público, paginado + busca)
GET {{baseUrl}}/services?page=1&limit=10&search=terapia

### 5.4 GET /services/:id (público, include do profissional)
GET {{baseUrl}}/services/{{serviceId}}

### 5.5 PATCH /services/:id pelo dono (200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "priceCents": 20000
}

### 5.6 PATCH /services/:id por não-dono (403)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer SEU_OUTRO_TOKEN_AQUI
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "priceCents": 1
}

### 5.7 DELETE /services/:id pelo dono (204) — soft delete
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 6. APPOINTMENTS — CRUD com ownership + ADMIN vê todos
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 6.1 POST /appointments (201) — data no futuro
# @name createAppointment
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "scheduledAt": "2026-12-01T14:00:00.000Z",
  "notes": "Primeira consulta"
}

@appointmentId = {{createAppointment.response.body.id}}

### 6.2 POST /appointments com data no passado (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "scheduledAt": "2020-01-01T10:00:00.000Z"
}

### 6.3 POST /appointments sem token (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "scheduledAt": "2026-12-15T10:00:00.000Z"
}

### 6.4 POST /appointments com serviço inexistente (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "service-id-inexistente",
  "scheduledAt": "2026-12-15T10:00:00.000Z"
}

### 6.5 GET /appointments — USER vê só os próprios
GET {{baseUrl}}/appointments?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 6.6 GET /appointments — ADMIN vê todos
GET {{baseUrl}}/appointments?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6.7 GET /appointments/:id pelo dono (200, include de service + user)
GET {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{appointmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 6.8 GET /appointments/:id por não-dono (403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{appointmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer SEU_OUTRO_TOKEN_AQUI

### 6.9 PATCH /appointments/:id pelo dono — confirmar
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{appointmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CONFIRMED",
  "notes": "Confirmado por e-mail"
}

### 6.10 DELETE /appointments/:id pelo dono — soft delete + status CANCELLED (204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{appointmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
